error[E0277]: `acvus_extern::Slice<acvus_extern::Owned<__R>, __R>` does not cross the boundary as one of the runtime's values
 --> tests/compile_fail/slice_by_value.rs:6:1
  |
6 | #[extern_fn(effect = pure)]
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the trait `OneValue<__R>` is not implemented for `acvus_extern::Slice<acvus_extern::Owned<__R>, __R>`
  |
  = note: a slice crosses as the two registers it occupies and is no value of the language: it is a result, never a parameter, a field, or a container's element (RFC-0047 amended).
  = help: the following other types implement trait `OneValue<Rt>`:
            `()` implements `OneValue<__Rt>`
            `Arr<T, N>` implements `OneValue<Rt>`
            `Erased<R, T>` implements `OneValue<R>`
            `Fn0<R, E, Rt>` implements `OneValue<Rt>`
            `Fn1<A, R, E, Rt>` implements `OneValue<Rt>`
            `Fn2<A, B, R, E, Rt>` implements `OneValue<Rt>`
            `Fn3<A, B, C, R, E, Rt>` implements `OneValue<Rt>`
            `Spec<T>` implements `OneValue<Rt>`
          and $N others
  = note: required for `ByValue<acvus_extern::Slice<acvus_extern::Owned<__R>, __R>>` to implement `for<'a> Arg<'a, __R>`
  = note: this error originates in the attribute macro `extern_fn` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)
